From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yah <yah@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:50:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 55/70] 0061-loom-sticky-status-writes-skip-issue-order

Loom: the physical issuer orders sticky status writes (OR-accumulating flags such as srFPFlags) like ordinary
writes, though the schedule graph already treats them as commutative; a softmax MAC waited 4 cycles on an earlier FP op's flag
write. GPU sets byte-identical; changes the NPU split's 27 images (NPU gate: pp2048 window 00 bit-identical);
NPU attention one core 680.4 -> 672.4 cycles a body, O exact.

(cherry picked from commit d08faaf66bbe4cbb795a2781e9ace52f55bd48fe)
---
 .../src/loom/codegen/low/schedule/physical_issue.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/schedule/physical_issue.c b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/schedule/physical_issue.c
index 2315edb233..bfdd41e2c9 100644
--- a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/schedule/physical_issue.c
+++ b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/schedule/physical_issue.c
@@ -162,6 +162,11 @@ static bool loom_low_physical_issue_events_fit(
         for (uint16_t c = 0; c < consumer->operand_count; ++c) {
           const loom_low_operand_t* rhs =
               loom_low_descriptor_operand(descriptor_set, consumer, c);
+          if (iree_all_bits_set(
+                  lhs->flags & rhs->flags,
+                  LOOM_LOW_OPERAND_FLAG_COMMUTATIVE_STATE_UPDATE)) {
+            continue;
+          }
           if (!loom_low_physical_events_require_separation(
                   schedule_model, lhs->read_event_id, rhs->write_event_id) &&
               !loom_low_physical_events_require_separation(
@@ -222,6 +227,15 @@ uint32_t loom_low_physical_issue_register_ready_cycle(
       const loom_low_operand_t* operand =
           loom_low_descriptor_operand(descriptor_set, descriptor, j);
       const uint16_t physical_register = instructions[i].physical_registers[j];
+      // Sticky status writes accumulate (OR) into their register, so they
+      // need no order among themselves; reads still wait for every write.
+      if (iree_any_bit_set(operand->flags,
+                           LOOM_LOW_OPERAND_FLAG_COMMUTATIVE_STATE_UPDATE)) {
+        cycle = iree_max(cycle, loom_low_schedule_event_frontier_query(
+                                    &issue->events, physical_register,
+                                    operand->read_event_id));
+        continue;
+      }
       cycle = iree_max(cycle, loom_low_schedule_event_frontier_query(
                                   &issue->events, physical_register,
                                   operand->read_event_id));
